-- title:
--   G Hat Reverse Half Product Sum Adjoint Mul Le One
-- statement:
--   **The reversed G-hat half-product is also a contraction.**
--
--   Let $(m,q,d)$ have a field model and let $F$ be a slice-indexed polynomial family. For a point tuple $\mathbf x$ of length $r$, write $\widetilde H_r(\mathbf x,\mathbf g)$ for the reversed ordered product of the completed slice effects.
--
--   For every $r\in\mathbb N$ and every $\mathbf x\in\mathbb{F}_q^r$,
--
--   $$
--   \sum_{\mathbf g}\widetilde H_r(\mathbf x,\mathbf g)^{\dagger}\widetilde H_r(\mathbf x,\mathbf g)\le I.
--   $$
--
--   This reverse-order normalization bound is used in the move-back and commutation steps of the half-sandwich chain.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.gHatReverseHalfProduct_sum_adjoint_mul_le_one`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
